WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.035
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.071
You're here! You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:09.075
♪♪

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.743
Well, guys,
I want to say congrats

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.345 line:0%
to the Cincinnati Bengals
and Los Angeles Rams

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:16.049 line:0%
on advancing to Super Bowl LVI.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.283 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.085
-Wow!
-Before the season,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:22.722
the Bengals' odds of winning
the Super Bowl were 150-1.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.491
-Ooh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.059
To give you an idea,
there are better odds

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.528
of finding a rapid test at CVS.
-Really?

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.563
[ Laughter ]
Than going to the Super Bowl.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.365
-Wow!
[ Applause ]

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.100
-That's true.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.334
"I'm sorry."
-"Nope."

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.337
-"Nope."

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.205
And this is crazy.
The Super Bowl is being played

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.441
in Los Angeles
at the Rams' home stadium.

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:43.843
[ Cheers ]

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.877
That's right.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.080
Even NFL players
are working from home.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.515
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:50.783
That's right.
We're two weeks away

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.585
from the game,
and experts are wondering,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.987
if a Super Bowl doesn't have
Tom Brady,

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.522
can it still be called
the Super Bowl?

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.591
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.993
I don't know.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.428
But this is the Bengals'
first Super Bowl appearance

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.931
since the '80s.
-Ooh.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.766
-A lot has changed since then.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.802
Back then, inflation was high,
there was tension with Russia,

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.671
and our president
was in his late 70s.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:16.575
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.878
Oh, and I saw that during
the Bengals/Chiefs games --

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.413
This just made me laugh.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.614
Did you see the announcements
over at CBS?

00:01:22.614 --> 00:01:24.250
-Oh, yeah.
-They have a great crew.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.286
They're awesome over there.
But at CBS, they're doing

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:29.389
the halftime, talking about
the stats and all that stuff.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.557
But they were just
in the worst spot

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:34.260
you could possibly be
on the field to talk.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.494
But take a look
at the halftime report.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:36.496
Look at this.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.331
-...as we welcome
Grammy-nominated

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:42.769
singer-songwriter Walker Hayes!

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.105
-...this game...
[ Country music plays loudly ]

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.140
They score, they go down...

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.409
[ Music drowning out dialogue ]

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:55.515
-At what point do you consider
blitzing Patrick Mahomes?!

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.949
-I have no idea
what you just said!

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:58.584
I can't hear a thing
anybody is saying!

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.086
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.887
The speakers
are right behind them!

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.956
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.558
It's the first football game
where the announcers

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.460
got concussions.
Unbelievable.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.730
Meanwhile, the big football
story from this weekend

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.398
wasn't the games.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:16.602 line:0%
On Saturday, ESPN reported
that Tom Brady is retiring.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:17.870 line:0%
But then --
[ Cheers ]

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.672 line:0%
But then,
conflicting reports came out

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.241
that said
Brady hasn't decided yet.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.709
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.544
This is what happens
when you let the CDC

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:27.246
announce your retirement.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:30.115
You just don't know --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:33.519
6 feet, 3 feet, 5 days...

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:34.853
[ Applause ]

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:36.789
Brady was like, "I just
wanted to see who was happy

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.959
so I can destroy them."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.427
Let's switch gears.
Over the weekend,

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.330
former president Trump
held a rally in Texas

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.499 line:0%
where he talked about
running for President

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.867 line:0%
and said that if he won,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:51.237 line:0%
he might pardon
the January 6th rioters.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.305
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.839
Even the rioters were like,
"Oh, no,

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:57.509
I don't think he can say that."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.578
Yeah, there's no way --
no better way to announce

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:02.081
a presidential run than saying,
"I'll empty the jails."

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:07.319
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:10.289
Well, the East Coast
is recovering

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:12.758
from a massive blizzard
that hit this weekend.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.594
Boston actually got one of its
biggest snowstorms ever,

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:17.397
but that didn't stop people
from going out.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.631
Watch this.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.066 line:0%
-Have you heard the news
about Tom Brady?

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.902 line:0%
-Yes.
-What do you make of all that?

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.203 line:0%
-I don't know. I don't know.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.972 line:0%
Is Gronk next then, I guess?

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.673 line:0%
-I thought he had
a couple more years, maybe.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.274 line:0%
-Where are you guys
trying to go right now?

00:03:29.274 --> 00:03:31.210 line:0%
-We're trying to find
an open Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.612 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.246 line:0%
[ Rim shot ]
-Can't find them.

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:36.015 line:0%
-Come on!
-No, dude --

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.419
-Come on!
-That's real.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.354
-Oh, my God.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.989
-We did not do anything
to that tape.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.658
That is real.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.226
Tom Brady, Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.994
If they snuck in David Ortiz,

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.929
they would have summoned
the ghost of Sam Adams.

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:54.533
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.670
How Boston is that?
Fantastic.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.105
[ Applause ]

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.974
You might have a problem
when you're willing to put on

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.177
ski goggles just to get
a pineapple Coolatta.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.612
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:07.980
But they weren't the only ones

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.315
who braved
the weekend's blizzard.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.817
I saw that a couple
in Rhode Island

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:14.053
actually got married outside
during the storm.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.788
Here's the happy couple there
right there.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.756
Yeah.
And this is real.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:20.493
Here's everyone
who showed up to the wedding.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:23.162
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.963
You know it's cold when your
"something blue"

00:04:24.963 --> 00:04:27.266
are your guests.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.468
And finally, a man who lives
on a lake in Canada

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:32.004
snapped a photo of a figure
that formed when waves

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.507
splashed onto the shore
and froze around a lamp post.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.075
People are saying it looks like
the Grim Reaper.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.543
Take a look at this.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.079
-Ooh.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.581
-Everyone thought it was
the Grim Reaper

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:44.249
until they heard Grandpa
whisper, "Help. Help me."

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:46.652
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.320 line:0%
After days of speculation,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.924 line:0%
today NFL superstar Tom Brady
officially retired.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.092 line:0%
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.862 line:0%
Yeah. Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.197
Yeah. Yeah, when they said
everyone is quitting their jobs

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.265
during the pandemic,
they meant everybody.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.265
-Wow.

00:05:00.265 --> 00:05:02.768
-Yeah. To celebrate retirement,

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:06.372
Brady ate one carb
and instantly gained 40 pounds.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.474
Unbelievable. I've never seen
anything like it.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.608
But this is amazing.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:10.810
Brady is walking away with

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.113
the most Super Bowl appearances,
wins, and MVPs.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.149
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.553
It's strange to say,

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.488
but he's basically
the NFL's Meryl Streep.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.756
-Oh.

00:05:24.756 --> 00:05:26.325
-I think it was time to go,
though, seriously.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.693
You know you've been around
a long time

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:30.563
when you debuted the same year
as "The Thong Song."

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.333
That's true.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.469
That's right -- right now,
Brady's backup in Tampa

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.172
is Googling where to buy
a football helmet.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.074
Let's switch gears.

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:45.410 line:0%
Apparently, former president
Trump's advisers

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.014 line:0%
have convinced him to
stop promoting vaccines

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.150 line:0%
because they're worried it could
alienate his supporters.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.053
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.187
Don't worry.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.089
To win back his
non-science supporters,

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.292
Trump is going to stare
into an eclipse again.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:07.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.267
That's right --
Trump is desperate.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.802
Right now, he's like,
"I'll do anything

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.772
in this whole flat world
to win you guys back."

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:16.976
Hey, guys, listen to this.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.111
Yesterday,
officials caught a chicken

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:22.948
trying to sneak
into the Pentagon.

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.484
No one really knows
what happened.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:26.718
The story is so bizarre,

00:06:26.718 --> 00:06:28.888
it actually inspired me
to write a tiny song.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.923
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:40.933
♪ There's a chicken at the
Pentagon, and no one knows why ♪

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:44.703
♪ Are you a normal clucker
or an undercover spy? ♪

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:48.407
♪ A chicken at the Pentagon,
and we're at a loss ♪

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:52.344
♪ Should we throw you in a
prison or some barbecue sauce? ♪

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:56.315
♪ A chicken at the Pentagon,
oh, what a crisis ♪

00:06:56.315 --> 00:07:00.152
♪ You get 25 to life
or 11 herbs and spices ♪

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:03.723
♪ Pentagon chicken,
you have our attention ♪

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.390
♪ You're raisin' our suspicion ♪

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.460
♪ 'Cause you do not have
permission ♪

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.428
♪ Our government's
panic-stricken ♪

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:11.596
♪ Their heart rates
have quickened ♪

00:07:11.596 --> 00:07:17.670
♪ Were you on a mission or are
you just finger-licking good? ♪

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.705
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:24.877
Thank you.

00:07:28.914 --> 00:07:31.050
Back to the monologue.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.687
Some business news.

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:38.690 line:0%
Tesla just released and sold out
of a new product

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.826 line:0%
called the TeslaMic,

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:44.130 line:0%
which is a set of karaoke
microphones for their cars.

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.032
It's gonna be weird
when drivers get pulled over

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:48.300
and they're like...

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.338
[ Auto-tuned ]
♪ What's the problem, Officer? ♪

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:57.309
♪ I thought
the speed limit was 55 ♪

00:07:57.309 --> 00:07:59.345
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:05.151
Oh, this is cool, too.

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:06.685
I saw that Jason Momoa
is joining

00:08:06.685 --> 00:08:08.820
the "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.290
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's amazing.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.259
And Vin Diesel
is so excited about it,

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:16.061
he actually made his own teaser
trailer for the next movie.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:17.763
Vin made this. Check this out.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.131 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.634
-There's nothing
more important than family.

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.136
And families get stronger
when you add a new person

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.105
to the family.

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:29.642
Jason Momoa is leaving
his fish family behind

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:32.344
to join us, his land family.

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:35.247
But the fish
are still his family.

00:08:35.247 --> 00:08:37.483
The sharks are family.

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.885
The dolphins are family.

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:44.356
Anything in the ocean is family,
even the boats.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:48.193
"Fast &amp; Furious 10:
Norwegian Cruise Line."

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:49.495
-Oh, interesting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:51.930
Wow! That's what it's about?

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.666
That's what it's -- Amazing.
-Wow!

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:55.902
-Some TV news.

00:08:55.902 --> 00:08:57.803 line:0%
Paramount+
just started production on

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:00.206 line:0%
a "Grease" prequel series called

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:02.675 line:0%
"Grease:
Rise of the Pink Ladies."

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.410
Yeah. It takes place before
the movie "Grease,"

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.613
so in this one,
the actors are only 45.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.081
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:14.720
-[As Travolta] Geez, Sandy,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.921
I can't believe
I'm in high school.

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:17.589
It's, like, crazy.

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:19.458
♪♪

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:22.627
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.627 --> 00:09:24.029
-"My hip."
-Yeah, I know. Yeah.

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:25.363
My hip broke.

00:09:25.363 --> 00:09:30.535
Yo, I can't believe I gotta
get hip surgery, right.

00:09:30.535 --> 00:09:32.537
[Normal voice] Guys,
there was a new episode of

00:09:32.537 --> 00:09:33.539
"The Bachelor" last night.

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:34.740
You know we love
"The Bachelor" here.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.474
And it was a pretty
intense showdown between

00:09:36.474 --> 00:09:37.977
Elizabeth and Shenae.

00:09:37.977 --> 00:09:39.712
Now, the show
can get pretty emotional,

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:40.979
so I thought we could help.

00:09:40.979 --> 00:09:42.581
So here's that moment revoiced

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:45.384
with the least-emotional person
we know, Siri.

00:09:45.384 --> 00:09:50.322
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:53.526
-[Whispering]
Let's get Siri-ous.

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:57.462
-I was upset. I'm mad.
I'm angry.

00:09:57.462 --> 00:09:59.932
In the house,
you make me uncomfortable.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.100
You're toxic.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.169
-Can you define a circumstance
of bullying?

00:10:03.169 --> 00:10:04.403
-Sounds silly, but you made

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.705
shrimp the other day, right?

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:06.772
You asked if I wanted some.

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:08.073
I was like, "Wow.
She is being really nice.

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:09.208
I'm going to take some shrimp.

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:10.442
Me and Eliza made some shrimp,

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:12.078
and I'm like, "Hey,
let me exchange the offer.

00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:14.846
Let me see if these girls in
the hot tub want some shrimp."

00:10:14.846 --> 00:10:16.481
-Does this sound like
bullying to you?

00:10:16.481 --> 00:10:17.616
-Please, Elizabeth.

00:10:17.616 --> 00:10:19.351
No one turns
back to even say just,

00:10:19.351 --> 00:10:20.719
"Shenae, no, thank you."

00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:22.821
-I wasn't outside when
you offered people shrimp.

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:24.322
-You were in the hot tub.

00:10:24.322 --> 00:10:26.191
-I have been nothing but kind
and respectful to you

00:10:26.191 --> 00:10:27.792
in the house, and as soon as
Clayton comes around,

00:10:27.792 --> 00:10:29.127
all of a sudden,
you have an issue.

00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:31.664
-I-I just need a -- I'm going to
step away for a second.

00:10:31.664 --> 00:10:32.965
-Okay.

00:10:32.965 --> 00:10:35.200
-Elizabeth looks like
Cruella de Vil.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.269
Where's your Dalmatians, bitch?

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:39.438
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Whoa.

00:10:42.441 --> 00:10:45.277
-"I was in the hot tub
when you offered shrimp."

00:10:45.277 --> 00:10:47.312
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:50.082
"I was in the hot tub
when you offered shrimp."

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:52.083
-Can you get me some shrimp?

00:10:52.083 --> 00:10:54.654
-I didn't know you had shrimp.
I was in the hot tub.

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:58.557
It's the best.

00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:00.192 line:0%
Guys, I read that the
world's top producer of

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.060 line:0%
mozzarella cheese
says that it expects

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.897 line:0%
shipping delays
to last all year.

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:07.433
Meanwhile, Papa John's
released a statement that said,

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:09.902
"Yeah, this doesn't
affect us whatsoever."

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:14.506 line:0%
And, finally, in an effort to
save money on cleaning crews,

00:11:14.506 --> 00:11:17.543 line:0%
a city in Sweden
is using crows to pick up

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:20.112 line:0%
cigarette butts off the streets.

00:11:20.112 --> 00:11:22.681
I guess some birds
are destined for the Pentagon,

00:11:22.681 --> 00:11:25.984
while others are stuck
picking up old cigarettes.

00:11:25.984 --> 00:11:29.488
Today is Groundhog Day.
Yeah. That's right.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.690
We spend all year telling people
to trust science

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.692
then ask a large rodent
to predict the weather.

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:35.327
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:36.928
Yep, this morning,
Punxsutawney Phil

00:11:36.928 --> 00:11:38.897
predicted six more weeks
of winter.

00:11:38.897 --> 00:11:40.131
[ Audience groans ]

00:11:40.131 --> 00:11:42.434
Asked why, Phil said,
"'Cause it's February."

00:11:42.434 --> 00:11:45.003
[ Laughter ]

00:11:45.003 --> 00:11:46.805
"You guys
have calendars up there?"

00:11:46.805 --> 00:11:48.273
Meanwhile, in New York,

00:11:48.273 --> 00:11:50.075
we have a groundhog,
and this is real.

00:11:50.075 --> 00:11:52.778
In New York, we have a groundhog
named Staten Island Chuck.

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:54.079
[ Laughter ]
It's true.

00:11:54.079 --> 00:11:56.214
And he predicted early spring.
-Oh.

00:11:56.214 --> 00:11:57.916
-He's just like
Punxsutawney Phil,

00:11:57.916 --> 00:11:59.985
but he wears a gold chain
and smokes a vape pen.

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:01.286
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.286 --> 00:12:03.288
"Yeah, spring."
[ Clears throat ]

00:12:03.288 --> 00:12:04.789
Well, this made me laugh.

00:12:04.789 --> 00:12:08.527
On Sunday, Queen Elizabeth will
celebrate 70 years as monarch,

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:10.829
but more than 10,000 souvenirs

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:14.300
marking her platinum jubilee
actually has a typo.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.902
This is real.
It says, "Platinum Jubbly."

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.137
[ Laughter ]
10,000.

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.337
Look at this. This is real.

00:12:19.337 --> 00:12:21.139
Check it out. Zoom in.

00:12:21.139 --> 00:12:23.175
-Ohh.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.676
-The Queen was not happy
with the plates.

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:26.411
For the rest of the day,
her office sounded like

00:12:26.411 --> 00:12:27.646
a Greek wedding.
[ Glass breaking ]

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:30.616
"Opa!"
[ Laughter ]

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:32.351
Some sports news --
today, the Washington

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:35.620 line:0%
Football Team finally announced
their new name.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.322
Yep, unfortunately,
due to a typo,

00:12:37.322 --> 00:12:39.224
they're going to be called
the Washington Jubblys.

00:12:39.224 --> 00:12:41.360
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.462
-Actually, Washington changed
their name to the Commanders.

00:12:44.462 --> 00:12:45.798
They made
the announcement today,

00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:47.232
but the name was actually leaked
last night

00:12:47.232 --> 00:12:48.701
when a news helicopter

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:51.737
spotted it on a banner
inside the stadium.

00:12:51.737 --> 00:12:53.939
Take a look at this.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.340
-Yeah, going out there,

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.845
and they just kind of zoom in,
and then they saw that.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:03.481
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.481 --> 00:13:05.350
News director was like,
"Uh, what else have you been

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.619
looking at with that camera,
Lou?"

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:10.789
[ Laughter ]

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:13.091
Every creep with a drone was
like, "Damn, way to up the game.

00:13:13.091 --> 00:13:14.926
That's not bad, not bad."
[ Laughter ]

00:13:14.926 --> 00:13:16.628
And today, there's another
football story

00:13:16.628 --> 00:13:18.063
everyone's talking about.

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:21.533 line:0%
Former Miami Dolphins coach
Brian Flores is suing the NFL

00:13:21.533 --> 00:13:22.734 line:0%
and three teams, claiming that

00:13:22.734 --> 00:13:25.404 line:0%
their hiring practices
are racist.

00:13:25.404 --> 00:13:26.939
Right now
NFL coaches are so white,

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:28.740
when they win the Super Bowl,
they're like,

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.075
"I'm going to Vineyard Vines!"

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:32.744
[ Laughter ]

00:13:32.744 --> 00:13:34.947 line:0%
Listen to this, guys --
NASA just announced that it will

00:13:34.947 --> 00:13:37.348 line:0%
retire the
International Space Station

00:13:37.348 --> 00:13:39.351 line:0%
in 2031 by crashing it

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.654 line:0%
into a remote part
of the Pacific Ocean.

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:43.088 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:46.058
Plan was put together by the
new head of NASA, Vin Diesel.

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:48.560
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.196
Wouldn't it be safer
to just leave it in space?

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:53.832
I know there's plenty of room.
It's called space.

00:13:53.832 --> 00:13:56.168
[ Laughter ]

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:58.137
People like, "I need space."
That is space.

00:13:58.137 --> 00:14:00.105
[ Laughter ]

00:14:00.105 --> 00:14:02.174
Hey, get this -- I read that
malls across the country

00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:04.109
have been filling
empty retail spaces

00:14:04.109 --> 00:14:06.678
with surgery centers.
-Oh.

00:14:06.678 --> 00:14:08.781
-That explains the store
I saw the other day

00:14:08.781 --> 00:14:10.449
called Appendectomy &amp; Fitch.

00:14:10.449 --> 00:14:12.318
[ Laughter ]
Now I get it.

00:14:12.318 --> 00:14:14.553
[ Laughter ]

00:14:14.553 --> 00:14:17.022
And, finally, a man in Canada
spent three days

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:19.725
building a giant snow bear
in his backyard

00:14:19.725 --> 00:14:22.093
as an early Valentine surprise
for his wife.

00:14:22.093 --> 00:14:23.929
[ Audience "Awws" ]
Take a look at this thing.

00:14:23.929 --> 00:14:26.231
[ Laughter ]

00:14:26.231 --> 00:14:28.366
Yeah, when he said, "Surprise!"
she was like,

00:14:28.366 --> 00:14:31.837
"Doug, I watched you
make this for three days."

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:34.138
The 2022 Beijing Winter Olympics

00:14:34.138 --> 00:14:35.907
are officially under way.

00:14:35.907 --> 00:14:37.876
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:14:37.876 --> 00:14:40.145
♪♪

00:14:40.145 --> 00:14:42.547
I love the Winter Olympics
because it features

00:14:42.547 --> 00:14:43.983
the last people on Earth

00:14:43.983 --> 00:14:46.918
who stuck to their
new year's resolutions.

00:14:46.918 --> 00:14:49.254
At this year's games,
there are 91 countries,

00:14:49.254 --> 00:14:52.858
109 events, and 1,000 chances to
hear the person next to you say,

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:55.560
"I could do that."

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.663
But tonight was the big
opening ceremony, and it was --

00:14:58.663 --> 00:15:00.632
It's fun, because the only place
you see all the countries

00:15:00.632 --> 00:15:03.335
get together are the Olympics,
the United Nations,

00:15:03.335 --> 00:15:05.537
and International
House of Pancakes.

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:07.072
So it's exciting.

00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:09.174
I read that the official motto
of the Winter Games

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:12.310 line:0%
is "Together for
a Shared Future."

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:14.346 line:0%
Yeah, when asked where
they got it from, China said,

00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:17.015 line:0%
"A Verizon commercial."

00:15:17.015 --> 00:15:19.651
Meanwhile, the Winter Olympics
have an official mascot.

00:15:19.651 --> 00:15:21.487
Did you see him?
Named Bing Dwen Dwen.

00:15:21.487 --> 00:15:22.587
Here he is.

00:15:22.587 --> 00:15:24.356
-[ Audience awws ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:15:24.356 --> 00:15:27.292
Looks like something you'd win
at a rest-stop claw machine.

00:15:27.292 --> 00:15:29.194
[ Laughter ]

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:32.331
Well, I saw that every Olympic
sport has its own unique logo

00:15:32.331 --> 00:15:33.798
designed for the Games.

00:15:33.798 --> 00:15:35.867
For example,
here's cross-country skiing.

00:15:35.867 --> 00:15:39.237
Yep, and it turns out, while
these are official Olympic logos

00:15:39.237 --> 00:15:41.406
for Olympic events,
they're also unofficial logos

00:15:41.406 --> 00:15:42.808
for other things.
-Really?

00:15:42.808 --> 00:15:44.509
-I'll show you what I mean.
Here's another logo.

00:15:44.509 --> 00:15:46.712
Officially, it's speed skating.

00:15:46.712 --> 00:15:50.015 line:0%
Unofficially, it's your aunt who
just found out about dabbing.

00:15:50.015 --> 00:15:52.050 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.519 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:15:54.519 --> 00:15:57.956 line:0%
Here's -- Here's the next logo.

00:15:57.956 --> 00:15:59.791 line:0%
Officially, it's luge.

00:15:59.791 --> 00:16:03.028 line:0%
Unofficially, it's trying to
fit in your jeans from 2019.

00:16:03.028 --> 00:16:04.262 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:16:04.262 --> 00:16:06.198 line:0%
[ Steve pops cheek, squeaks ]

00:16:06.198 --> 00:16:09.667
Here's another logo.
Officially, it's figure skating.

00:16:09.667 --> 00:16:12.504 line:0%
Unofficially, it's that annoying
show-off at yoga class.

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:14.706 line:0%
It's like, "All right, yeah."

00:16:14.706 --> 00:16:18.177
Here's the next logo.
Officially, it's skeleton.

00:16:18.177 --> 00:16:20.412 line:0%
Unofficially,
it's Spotify's stock price.

00:16:20.412 --> 00:16:22.114 line:0%
That's interesting.
-Oh, wow.

00:16:22.114 --> 00:16:24.383
They have a logo for that?!
-That's the logo for it.

00:16:24.383 --> 00:16:27.385
-Wow!
-Finally, here's one last logo.

00:16:27.385 --> 00:16:30.021
Officially,
it's short track speed skating.

00:16:30.021 --> 00:16:34.126 line:0%
Unofficially, it's racing to get
the last rapid test at CVS.

00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:36.094 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:16:36.094 --> 00:16:40.965 line:0%
♪♪

00:16:40.965 --> 00:16:43.335
Hey, I heard it's going to be
the first Winter Olympics

00:16:43.335 --> 00:16:46.638
that relies almost entirely
on fake snow.

00:16:46.638 --> 00:16:48.072
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:16:48.072 --> 00:16:50.242
They're going to create
over 1 million cubic meters

00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:54.112
of fake snow, or roughly one
Hallmark Christmas movie.

00:16:54.112 --> 00:16:55.880
Well, get this --
a company in China

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.582 line:0%
just unveiled plans for a plane

00:16:57.582 --> 00:17:00.319 line:0%
that can fly
7,000 miles per hour,

00:17:00.319 --> 00:17:02.153 line:0%
which means that you can go
from New York to Beijing

00:17:02.153 --> 00:17:04.022 line:0%
in 60 minutes.

00:17:04.022 --> 00:17:05.857
Yeah, the company said
it's perfectly safe

00:17:05.857 --> 00:17:07.826
and that your eyeballs
return to their sockets

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:09.695
within hours of landing.

00:17:09.695 --> 00:17:11.429
[ Laughter ]

00:17:11.429 --> 00:17:12.964
Some business news.

00:17:12.964 --> 00:17:14.233 line:0%
I saw that Costco is once again

00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:17.703 line:0%
selling a 5-pound tub
of Pillsbury cookie dough.

00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:19.738 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:21.406 --> 00:17:23.942
Imagine picking up a 4-pound tub
of cookie dough and going,

00:17:23.942 --> 00:17:26.645
"Nah, I wanted the bigger one."

00:17:26.645 --> 00:17:29.281
Yep, Americans saw 5 pounds
of cookie dough and said,

00:17:29.281 --> 00:17:31.883
"Do you believe in miracles?!
Yes!"

00:17:31.883 --> 00:17:35.187
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:35.187 --> 00:17:36.622
"Yes!"

00:17:36.622 --> 00:17:38.457
And finally, you guys,
we're all so excited

00:17:38.457 --> 00:17:40.125
that the Olympics are here,
and of course

00:17:40.125 --> 00:17:41.626
we're pumped
for all the big events,

00:17:41.626 --> 00:17:43.395
but there's one event
that doesn't always get

00:17:43.395 --> 00:17:44.863
the most attention.

00:17:44.863 --> 00:17:47.131
Until now. Take a look.

00:17:47.131 --> 00:17:50.669
[ Techno beat plays ]

00:17:50.669 --> 00:17:52.604
♪ You think
that all Olympic sports ♪

00:17:52.604 --> 00:17:54.406
♪ Are glory, gold, and fame,
they're not ♪

00:17:54.406 --> 00:17:57.509
♪ But there is one that stands
above that isn't playing games ♪

00:17:57.509 --> 00:17:59.744
♪ No more games, forget
the slopes, forget the ice ♪

00:17:59.744 --> 00:18:01.546
♪ No, I'm not in the mood,
not tonight ♪

00:18:01.546 --> 00:18:05.316
♪ 'Cause I want to sing about
tonight is doubles luge ♪

00:18:05.316 --> 00:18:08.920
♪ Two buds, one sled,
try to stay alive ♪

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.023
♪ Bodysuit skin tight,
spooning while we drive ♪

00:18:12.023 --> 00:18:14.293
♪ Spoon me,
first sprint, then slide ♪

00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:16.060
♪ The hard work never ends ♪

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:18.563
♪ We shoot through all the tubes
just like a colon cleanse ♪

00:18:18.563 --> 00:18:20.031
Ohh, ow!

00:18:20.031 --> 00:18:23.302
♪ Flying fast, making turns
in sync with my teammate ♪

00:18:23.302 --> 00:18:27.205
♪ I whisper in his ear,
"You're really doing great" ♪

00:18:27.205 --> 00:18:28.940
♪ Milliseconds for the win ♪

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.842
♪ We simply cannot lose,
don't lose ♪

00:18:30.842 --> 00:18:33.946
♪ Pelvis on pelvis,
that is doubles luge ♪

00:18:33.946 --> 00:18:35.213
♪ Again ♪

00:18:35.213 --> 00:18:38.050
♪ Pelvis on pelvis,
that is doubles luge ♪

